From: FIRERED project
Subject: [PATCH 14] Freeze legacy Unown form IDs before species expansion

Reference target: pret/pokefirered
Reference snapshot: c75f352304d529f6ba92d4f74b9cf8b5c3810788

FireRed stores Unown B through ? as graphics/form-only species IDs immediately
above the retail NUM_SPECIES boundary. Defining those IDs as NUM_SPECIES + n
makes them move when NUM_SPECIES is increased for later generations.

Freeze the legacy range at its retail values instead:

    retail NUM_SPECIES / SPECIES_EGG = 412
    Unown B..? = 413..439
    first safe expanded regular species ID = 440

Current retail values do not change. Future species imports must reserve
412..439 for Egg and the legacy Unown form slots and begin new regular species
at FIRERED_EXPANDED_SPECIES_START.

